Original commit body from df8d45a0a45477b93fb51aca6d06d1f1a38ba115:

Scala calls a parameterless method without parentheses
(Runtime.getRuntime.availableProcessors, System.currentTimeMillis) and
Kotlin reads a Java getter as a property (proc.inputStream). Neither
parsed as a call, so no edge existed for receiver typing to reach.

The grammar cannot tell such an access from a field read (System.out),
so it counts as a call only where a library-signature row or a
function/method io_primitives row says the owner declares that method
(jvm_implicit_imports.is_known_library_method). Kotlin tries getX / isX
(and an isX property's own name).

Measured against dev: sbt +150 calls edges, gatling +7, okhttp +1,
detekt 0; none lost. gatling ActorSystem.scala:36 and sbt
EvaluateTask.scala:223 now emit getRuntime + availableProcessors.

